Duplat & Tran-Ha site-index curves (1997 and subsequent)
--------------------------------------------------------
Reference: Duplat, P., Tran-Ha, M. (1997). "Modélisation de la
           croissance en hauteur dominante du chêne sessile
           (Quercus petraea Liebl) en France. Variabilité
           inter-régionale et effet de la période récente
           (1959-1993)." Annales des Sciences Forestières, 54(7),
           611-634. Companion publications by the same authors
           cover Quercus robur, Fagus sylvatica, Abies alba,
           Picea abies, Pinus sylvestris and Castanea sativa.
Authors  : P. Duplat and M. Tran-Ha (IFN / ONF).
License  : The site-index curves tabulated in
           inst/extdata/site_index_curves.csv are reconstituted
           from the published models of Duplat & Tran-Ha 1997
           and related publications. Redistribution within the
           `nemeton` R package is authorised by M. Tran-Ha
           (personal communication, April 2026). Downstream
           redistribution of the CSV by third parties must
           preserve the present attribution and cite the original
           publications.
           Parameters for Douglas (Pseudotsuga menziesii) come
           from DSF / IRSTEA publications; Pin maritime (Pinus
           pinaster) from IFN Landes technical notes; Peuplier
           cultivé (Populus sp.) from CNPF technical notes.
           Per-species source references are listed in
           data-raw/site_index_curves.R.
Usage    : Site-index estimation (P2 indicator) when a Canopy
           Height Model is available (spec 005 phase 2).

RAG knowledge corpus (spec 009.1)
---------------------------------
The retrieval-augmented knowledge base (E7, specs 009 / 009.1) is
declared by the manifest `inst/extdata/knowledge_corpus_v1.csv`, the
single source of truth for which documents may be ingested, under
which license, and with which ingestion strategy. The corpus itself
(embedded chunks) is NOT bundled with the package: it is rebuilt from
the manifest by `data-raw/build_knowledge_corpus.R`. Each document
carries its license in the `license` column; a document is only
full-text ingested once its license is personally confirmed
(`status = cleared`), per decision D5 of spec 009.1.

Sources currently declared in the manifest, by license class:
  - Project-own content (MIT): the 10 tutorials under inst/tutorials/
    and the internal specs — fully ingestible, no third-party rights.
  - Public domain / law: French Code forestier via Légifrance
    (https://www.legifrance.gouv.fr).
  - EU reusable: EU Forest Strategy COM(2021) 572 via EUR-Lex
    (reuse authorised, https://eur-lex.europa.eu).
  - Open Licence / Etalab 2.0: IGN BD Forêt® (see above); OFB guides
    CT88 / CT82 (https://espaces-naturels.fr); ONF and CNPF/CRPF
    regulatory documents (PSG, CBPS, RTG, SRGS, DRA/SRA) — Etalab or
    reusable administrative acts.
  - Free-use: IPCC 2019 Refinement, AFOLU volume
    (https://www.ipcc-nggip.iges.or.jp).
  - Explicit authorisation: Duplat & Tran-Ha site-index work (see the
    dedicated section above).
  - CC-BY (to confirm per source): Forrester et al. 2017, Larrieu
    et al. 2018, Monnet & Mermin 2014.
  - HAL deposits: Bontemps et al. 2006/2007/2009, Charru et al.
    2012/2017 (deposit license verified per record).
Copyrighted papers (e.g. Mouret et al. 2022, Fassnacht et al. 2016,
McCool et al. 1987, Beven & Kirkby 1979) are NEVER full-text ingested:
they are referenced abstract-only or link-only so the assistant can
cite them without redistributing protected text (spec 009.1 §5).

Each cited chunk surfaced in an AI perspective carries its source
document's attribution back to the user; the manifest's `license`
and `notes` columns are the audit trail.

RECONFORT oak-dieback models and Python glue
--------------------------------------------
Reference: Mouret, F., Morin, D., Martin, H., Planells, M.,
           Vincent-Barbaroux, C. (2023). "Toward an Operational
           Monitoring of Oak Dieback With Multispectral Satellite Time
           Series: A Case Study in Centre-Val De Loire Region of
           France." IEEE J-STARS. doi:10.1109/JSTARS.2023.3332420
Source   : https://framagit.org/fl.mouret/reconfort (branch main,
           commit 25198c9)
License  : Apache-2.0
Usage    : Random-Forest dieback models and the OSO 2021 deciduous
           mask (fetched on demand by `ensure_reconfort_model()` /
           `ensure_reconfort_oso_mask()`, spec 021 L2a/L2b.3) and the
           Python map-production glue vendored under
           `inst/python/reconfort/` (CRswir/CRre continuum-removal
           indices, GEODES download, IOTA² cfg generators, masking and
           continuous-score computation, plus the static IOTA² inputs
           under `iota2/`; spec 021 L2b.1–L2b.3). SYCOMORE programme,
           Université d'Orléans / CESBIO, funded by the Région
           Centre-Val de Loire.

Third-party attributions in source code
---------------------------------------
All data-source metadata (URLs, providers, licenses) are declared in
JSON configuration files under `inst/datasources/*.json` and read via
`get_country_config()` / `get_data_source()`.
